<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Surguja State</h1><p class="st-meta">1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.) · capital Ambikapur</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A large forest state of the Chota Nagpur plateau ruled by Rakshel Rajput Maharajas from Ambikapur.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Surguja was ruled by a Rakshel family whose traditions trace their arrival to the hill country of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a> centuries earlier. The register dates the state to around 1600. In the 18th century it came under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> pressure from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/nagpur-kingdom">Bhonsles of Nagpur</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharaja">Maharajas</a> governed a vast upland of sal forest, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurukh-people">Oraon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gond-people">Gond</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kawar-people">Kanwar</a> and other Adivasi communities forming much of the population. Under British paramountcy from 1818, Surguja was one of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chota-nagpur-plateau">Chota Nagpur</a> tributary states, transferred to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces</a> in 1905 and later to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-states-agency">Eastern States Agency</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Surguja merged into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces and Berar</a> in 1948, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>. Since 2000 its territory has been in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chhattisgarh">Chhattisgarh</a>, where Surguja is a district with its seat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ambikapur">Ambikapur</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/surguja-state.jpg" alt="Surguja State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Germenfer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Surguja_State.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1600 CE – 1948 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Ambikapur</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ramanuj Saran Singh Deo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Surgujia, Hindi</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>India</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Sarguja</dd></dl></aside></div>
